<p>The Merchants Hotel was among Mandan's earliest hotels. Built by {% person "henry-yunck" %}Henry{% endperson %} and {% person "philomena-knaus-yunck" %}Philomena Yunck{% endperson %}, it opened in January 1880 at 112 East Main Street and operated until 1920. The hotel stood between the early railroad depot and the Emerson Institute, later expanded as the Opera House. After the railroad opened a larger depot three blocks west in 1883, the Merchants primarily served railroad workers and immigrants.</p>

