<p>{% person "herman-yunck" %}Herman Yunck{% endperson %}, Henry's younger brother, was born in Richmond, Minnesota, in 1854. He moved to Mandan in 1881 and worked for druggist {% person "d-r-taylor" %}D. R. Taylor{% endperson %} and the Northern Pacific Railway. After several years aboard riverboats, he operated a saloon owned by Henry.</p>

<p>Henry died in April 1884. Herman married Philomena in 1886 and continued operating the hotel with her. Together, they raised six of Philomena's seven children. Herman was a charter member of the Mandan volunteer fire department and ran its Hook and Ladder Company. He died September 23, 1913.</p>

