<p>The hotel became a boardinghouse in 1920. Polish immigrant {% person "emil-block" %}Emil Block{% endperson %} moved from Bismarck, married the Yuncks' daughter {% person "willamina-minnie-yunck-block" %}Willamina—also called Minnie{% endperson %}—and opened a tailor shop in front. Philomena lived with her daughter and son-in-law until her death in 1925. After Block retired in 1953, Seeb's Shoe Repair occupied the shop, followed by Ray's Bootery.</p>

<p>In February 1965, firefighters spent three hours battling a major fire that began in the basement and spread in high winds to both adjacent commercial buildings. Firefighters rescued a family member. At the time, {% person "ray-mosbrucker" %}Ray Mosbrucker{% endperson %} owned and operated Ray's Bootery. Seeb's Shoe Repair and the vacant former Friesz Grocery building were also involved in the fire.</p>

<p>The Society thanks {% person "laine-pope" %}Laine Pope{% endperson %} for sharing information about her great-grandparents.</p>
